# NOTE: GitHub Pages does NOT honor this file. It exists for the day this
# site moves behind Cloudflare Pages, Netlify, or any CDN that reads _headers
# (or as a contract reference for whichever proxy is set up).
#
# The CSP actually in effect is generated per page by Astro's `security.csp`
# (see astro.config.mjs) and injected as a <meta http-equiv>, with per-script
# SHA-256 hashes rather than 'unsafe-inline'. Those hashes are per page, so this
# file cannot reproduce them — the policy below is deliberately the weaker,
# static equivalent, and a proxy serving it would be *loosening* script-src
# relative to the meta. If this file ever becomes live, drop script-src and
# style-src from it and let the meta own them; a header and a meta intersect, so
# the meta's hashes keep applying.
#
# What only a header can do, and what this file is really for:
# frame-ancestors, HSTS, X-Frame-Options, Permissions-Policy. See ADR 0008.

/*
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  X-Frame-Options: DENY
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
  Permissions-Policy: camera=(), microphone=(), geolocation=()
  Strict-Transport-Security: max-age=31536000; includeSubDomains; preload
  Content-Security-Policy: default-src 'self'; frame-ancestors 'none'; base-uri 'self'; form-action 'self'; font-src 'self'; img-src 'self' data:; connect-src 'self'

/_astro/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable
